      "text": "To find the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\) given \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the property of inverse matrices that states \\((\\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1} = (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{A})^{-1} = \\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\).\n\nFirst, we need to find \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\mathbf{A}\\). Since \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we multiply this matrix by itself:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTo perform the matrix multiplication, we calculate each element of the resulting matrix:\n\nThe element in the first row and first column is:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 4 - 5 = -1\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and second column is:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5 + 5 \\cdot (-3) = 10 - 15 = -5\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and first column is:\n\\[\n-1 \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot (-1) = -2 + 3 = 1\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and second column is:\n\\[\n-1 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-3) = -5 + 9 = 4\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the inverse of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\). To find the inverse of a 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\\), we use the formula:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \\frac{1}{ad - bc} \\begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\\\ -c & a \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor our matrix \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we have \\(a = -1\\), \\(b = -5\\), \\(c = 1\\), and \\(d = 4\\). The determinant is:\n\\[\nad - bc = (-1)(4) - (-5)(1) = -4 + 5 = 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the inverse is:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \\frac{1}{1} \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
